---@field value string The value to set on the record, exactly as given, including any prefix. Do not trim or reformat it: verification compares the published record against this string. Use the lowest TTL your provider allows until the domain is verified. Verification polls DNS, so a long TTL keeps a stale value cached and can burn the verification window on a value you have already corrected. Raise it afterwards if you want.
